CountSpatula wrote:

 > How about the protection racket?  Is it worthwhile
 > with the wizard, or should I just ignore that in
 > favour of dragon scales?

Since you want your wizard to become a dagger
flinging distance-slaughter machine, to preserve
spellpoints when there are few available maximum,
it's worth going through top level mines above Mines
Town at a slow march just to gain lots of encounters
with gnomes with stacks of daggers to add to the
PC's knapsack.

To keep your PC from meeting lots of "too tough"
monsters while doing this, it's best to keep XL as
low as possible.

The protection racket falls out of this set of
considerations naturally, so you might as well go
for it, but "going for it" means bankrupting a few
shops along the way, still at low XL, to build a
supply of zorkmids for bribing the priest.

=====

Another good hint is to go ahead and dress your PC
wizard temporarily in well enchanted armor for good
AC, from the plentiful supply in top levels mines,
and forego spellcasting (much) until your wizard is
expert at daggers and has a good sized stack of
them (to help avoid melee combat), preferably
blessed and eventually highly enchanted.

